A||||7||drednot||How do I replace a Fiero Clutch??||||11||
Z||000000||drednot||06-18-2001||05:46 PM||||I need a step by step procedure.  I have gotten quotes for $1,200 for a replacement.  Well, **** , I could get a new fiero for that much!  How hard could it be??  I guess I have to do it myself.  The clutch just won't dis-engage.  I keep having to jam / grind it into gear, and I have had to do this for about the last 3000 miles.  It has just gotten too hard to jam in now.  I have got to get this thing fixed.  BTW, 1985 Fiero 2.5, 5 speed, Hydraulics working 100%  Took measurement @ slave- 1 inch of travel, have steel pedal.||||reg||11
Z||000001||PBJ||06-18-2001||06:02 PM||||Check this out. If you have more questions just ask<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/010751.html" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/010751.html</A> <P><p>[This message has been edited by PBJ (edited 06-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||G-Nasty||06-18-2001||10:44 PM||||I've replaced the clutch disc and it was hard to "stab" the transmission with that clutch tool. My other car I took to a shop and they did it for about 600.<BR>They dropped the two rear cradle bolts which allowed them to swing the assembly down enough to get to transmission. The 5 speed getrag is easy once this is done-get a haynes manual and replace both disc and pressure plate-Good luck , because u gonna need it-||||reg||1
Z||000003||00lE||06-20-2001||11:28 AM||||Unless the clutch is slipping, it is much more likely to be a hydraulic problem.  But if you have already ruled that out there are some less costly reasons for difficult shifting:<P>Cracked or loose clutch release lever. (sometimes hard to see cracks without removal, a cast lever that is less prone to cracking replaced the older welded plate steel design on the Getrag, not sure about the Isuzu). <P>Incorrect shift cable adjustments.  Sometimes the adjusting bolt at the trans will loosen, or the clip at the shifter that holds the cable breaks.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by 00lE (edited 06-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Philphine||06-20-2001||11:32 AM||||thats where i am now. my shifting was getting really hard but would kind of come and go. tried to bleed it and it got worse. i noticed some seeping around the clutch shaft so i'm starting with changing the mc.||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||06-20-2001||11:44 AM||||theres a lot of work putting a clutch in, almost as bad as swapping engines. Shops around here will do it for about $600-700. Thats what I did last time, didnt have time to mess with it myself. Its worked great for over 2 years now, just OEM clutch.||||reg||1
